[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think more carefully about the math. Let me try a more theoretical [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mapproach.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mEquation: f(x) = f(h(x) + y) + f(x·f(y))·f(x+y), where h(x) = f(f(f(x))).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mKey: f(x) > f(h(x)+y) for all y > 0. So f(x) > f(t) for all t > h(x). (I)[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis means: for each x, the value f(x) strictly dominates f on (h(x), ∞).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mConsequence: f cannot have a maximum in the interior that is achieved. Actually,[0m[38;2;124;124;124mlet me think about whether f is injective.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSuppose f(a) = f(b) = v with a ≠ b. From (I), v > f(t) for all t > h(a) and v > [0m[38;2;124;124;124mf(t) for all t > h(b). So v > f(t) for all t > min(h(a), h(b)).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow apply the equation at x = a and x = b:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mv = f(h(a)+y) + f(a·f(y))·f(a+y)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mv = f(h(b)+y) + f(b·f(y))·f(b+y)[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo f(h(a)+y) + f(a·f(y))·f(a+y) = f(h(b)+y) + f(b·f(y))·f(b+y) for all y.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis is a constraint but doesn't immediately give a = b.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me try another angle. Let me see what happens with the substitution that [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mmakes the two terms relate.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me define u(x) = f(x) and try to find a relation by setting y such that h(x)[0m[38;2;124;124;124m+ y = x + y', i.e., relate the arguments.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, let me try to extract more from the equation by considering it as y [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mvaries.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor fixed x, as y varies over ℝ+:[0m
